      "claim": "A fused aromatic carbonyl compound (THA) reached peak brain levels of 1.8 µg/g in rats, demonstrating that fused bicyclic systems with multiple polar groups can still achieve meaningful CNS exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
