      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "3-Hydroxyindolin-2-one produced dose-dependent brain concentrations in mice, showing that oxidized indole/lactam analogs can cross the BBB.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C10"],
      "claim": "A larger isoindolinone-containing radiotracer showed no brain localization in mice, but its bulky piperazine/iodobenzyl substituents and much higher molecular weight limit transfer of this failure to the smaller query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "Atovaquone had CSF/plasma ratios below 1% in humans, showing that lipophilic fused-ring systems can fail to cross the BBB; however, its much higher molecular weight and different physicochemical profile make this a weak negative analogy for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
